---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { pick } from '../data/faq';
---
<Guide
  page="seerr"
  lede="Cupola is an app for Seerr, Overseerr and Jellyseerr on iPhone, Android and Mac. You get Discover, requests and approvals. Everyone else at home gets a simpler app to ask for things."
  screen="requests"
  services={['seerr', 'jellyfin', 'plex']}
  questions={pick('seerr', 'household', 'player', 'leaves')}
  related={['arr', 'stream', 'install']}
>
  <h2>For you, running the server</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Discover.</strong> Trending, a calendar, genres, networks, studios, people, moods and languages, plus the collections you only partly have.</li>
    <li><strong>Requests.</strong> Approve or decline from your phone, resolve issues, keep a watchlist.</li>
    <li><strong>One search.</strong> Seerr, Radarr, Sonarr, Jellyfin, Plex and Emby answer together, so you know if you already have it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>For everyone else at home</h2>
  <p>Family members sign in to Seerr with their own account (email, Jellyfin, Emby or Plex). They get a Cupola with three tabs: Home, Discover and their requests.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Plain status.</strong> <em>Waiting for approval</em>, <em>Downloading 62% · ready around 21:10</em>, <em>Ready to watch</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing technical.</strong> No API keys, no queues, no service names beyond Jellyfin, Plex and Emby.</li>
    <li><strong>Only what they can do.</strong> If the server would refuse it, the button is not there.</li>
    <li><strong>A widget and a notification.</strong> Their requests on the home screen, and <em>Ready to watch</em> when one arrives.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Inviting someone</h2>
  <p>In Seerr, <strong>Invite someone</strong> makes a link or a QR code with the server's address, never its API key. They install Cupola, open the link and sign in.</p>

  <h2>Not a player</h2>
  <p>Cupola tells you when something is ready. You watch it where you always do: Jellyfin, Plex, Emby or your TV.</p>
</Guide>
